{"ref":"BDB, שַׁכּוּל","hw":"שַׁכּוּל","html":"† <big><span dir=\"rtl\">שַׁכּוּל</span></big>  <strong>adj. bereaved, robbed of offspring (</strong>Ba <sup>§ 37 c</sup><strong>)</strong>;—especially <span dir=\"rtl\">דֹּב שׁ׳</span> <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 17:8\" href=\"/II_Samuel.17.8\">2 S 17:8</a>; <a data-ref=\"Hosea 13:8\" href=\"/Hosea.13.8\">Ho 13:8</a>; <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 17:12\" href=\"/Proverbs.17.12\">Pr 17:12</a> (sim. of fierceness); <span dir=\"rtl\">נְשֵׁיהֶם שַׁכֻּלוֹת</span> <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 18:21\" href=\"/Jeremiah.18.21\">Je 18:21</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">שַׁבֻּלָה אֵין בָּהֶם</span> <a data-ref=\"Song of Songs 4:2\" href=\"/Song_of_Songs.4.2\">Ct 4:2</a> (of flock, in sim.) = <a data-ref=\"Song of Songs 6:6\" href=\"/Song_of_Songs.6.6\">6:6</a>.","next":"BDB, שִׁכֻּלִים","prev":"BDB, שָׁכוּל"}